IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lpa-dates`

-- Legal Profession Act 2007 (Qld), Part 3.4 (costs disclosure and assessment) -- the seat-neutral core, in the Act's
-- own actors and terms: "the client", "the law practice", "the costs assessor", "the Supreme Court or the tribunal".
-- The focus is costs agreements (Division 5, ss 322-328), with the disclosure (Division 3), billing (Division 6) and
-- assessment (Division 7) rules a client meets around them, and the application rules of Division 2.
--
-- Each rule is preceded by the words of the section it encodes. Judgments the Act leaves to someone else (a principal
-- deciding "on reasonable grounds", a costs assessor being "satisfied", the court or tribunal being "satisfied the
-- agreement is not fair or reasonable") are inputs, or the answer is worded conditionally; none is decided here.
--
-- Not encoded: Division 8 (s 347, the cap on costs for a speculative personal injury claim). Its formula is an image
-- that the deposited text does not convert; see NOTES.md, finding 1.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Legal Profession Act 2007 (Qld), Part 3.4 -- costs`

§§ `Amounts (s 300)`

-- s 300 "disclosure threshold amount means-- (a) the amount prescribed by regulation for this definition; or (b) if no
-- amount is prescribed--$1,500." The Legal Profession Regulation 2017 is not deposited; the Act's own figure is used.
`the disclosure threshold amount (s 300)` MEANS 1500

-- s 300 "detailed disclosure threshold amount means-- (a) the amount prescribed by regulation ...; or (b) if no amount
-- is prescribed--$3,000." The Act's own figure, as above.
`the detailed disclosure threshold amount (s 300)` MEANS 3000

-- s 324(4) "the uplift fee must not exceed 25% of the legal costs, excluding disbursements, otherwise payable."
`the uplift cap (s 324(4))` MEANS 25%

-- s 342(2)(a) "on the assessment, the legal costs are reduced by 15% or more".
`the assessment reduction mark (s 342(2)(a))` MEANS 15%

§§ `Who is a sophisticated client (s 300, s 311(1)(c)-(d))`

-- s 300 "sophisticated client means a client to whom, because of section 311(1)(c) or (d), disclosure under section
-- 307B, 308 or 309(1) is not or was not required." s 311(1)(c) is a closed list of kinds of client (a law practice or
-- Australian legal practitioner, a public company, a large proprietary company, a financial services licensee, a
-- liquidator, a large professional partnership, a Minister or public authority, a bankruptcy trustee, and others);
-- (d) is costs agreed as a result of a tender process.
GIVEN `the client is of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs were agreed as a result of a tender process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a sophisticated client (s 300)` IF
        `the client is of a kind listed in s 311(1)(c)`
    OR  `the costs were agreed as a result of a tender process`

§§ `Does Part 3.4 apply (ss 302-304)`

DECLARE `Application answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the client first instructed the law practice in this jurisdiction (s 302)`
    `yes: by the client's acceptance of a written offer, or written notice, under s 303`
    `no: Part 3.4 has been displaced by the corresponding law of another jurisdiction (s 304)`
    `no: neither s 302 nor s 303 applies Part 3.4 on these facts`

DECLARE `Application facts` HAS
    `first instructed in Queensland`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `where first instructed cannot be decided`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `services mainly in Queensland or substantial connection` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accepted a written offer that Part 3.4 apply`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `gave written notice requiring Part 3.4`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice was more than 28 days after being told of the right` IS A BOOLEAN
    `services mainly elsewhere or substantial connection elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN
    `chose the other jurisdiction's law under its corresponding law` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 302 "This part applies to a matter if the client first instructs the law practice in relation to the matter in
-- this jurisdiction."
-- s 303(1) "This part applies to a matter if-- (a) either-- (i) this part does not currently apply to the matter; or
-- (ii) it is not possible to decide the jurisdiction in which the client first instructs ...; and (b) either or both of
-- the following-- (i) the legal services are or will be provided wholly or primarily in this jurisdiction; (ii) the
-- matter has a substantial connection with this jurisdiction; and (c) either-- (i) the client accepts ... a written
-- offer ...; or (ii) the client gives notice under subsection (2)(b) for the matter."
-- s 303(4) "A notice has no effect for subsection (2)(b) if it is given after the period of 28 days after the law
-- practice discloses to the client, under a corresponding law, information about the client's right to give notice".
-- s 304(2) "This part ceases to apply to the matter if-- (a) either or both of the following apply-- (i) the legal
-- services are or will be provided wholly or primarily in another jurisdiction; (ii) the matter has a substantial
-- connection with another jurisdiction; and (b) either-- (i) the client ... enters into an agreement ...; or (ii) the
-- client notifies ... that the client requires the corresponding provisions of the corresponding law to apply".
-- s 304(3) (a later s 303 agreement or notice re-applying the Part) is not encoded.
GIVEN `f` IS AN `Application facts`
GIVETH AN `Application answer`
`the Part 3.4 application answer (ss 302-304)` `f` MEANS
    IF `applies` AND `displaced`
    THEN `no: Part 3.4 has been displaced by the corresponding law of another jurisdiction (s 304)`
    ELSE IF `applies under s 302`
         THEN `yes: the client first instructed the law practice in this jurisdiction (s 302)`
         ELSE IF `applies under s 303`
              THEN `yes: by the client's acceptance of a written offer, or written notice, under s 303`
              ELSE `no: neither s 302 nor s 303 applies Part 3.4 on these facts`
    WHERE
        `applies under s 302` MEANS `f`'s `first instructed in Queensland`
        `notice has effect` MEANS
                `f`'s `gave written notice requiring Part 3.4`
            AND (NOT (`f`'s `the notice was more than 28 days after being told of the right`))
        `applies under s 303` MEANS
                ((NOT `applies under s 302`) OR `f`'s `where first instructed cannot be decided`)
            AND `f`'s `services mainly in Queensland or substantial connection`
            AND (`f`'s `accepted a written offer that Part 3.4 apply` OR `notice has effect`)
        `applies` MEANS `applies under s 302` OR `applies under s 303`
        `displaced` MEANS
                `f`'s `services mainly elsewhere or substantial connection elsewhere`
            AND `f`'s `chose the other jurisdiction's law under its corresponding law`

§§ `Costs disclosure (Division 3)`

DECLARE `Disclosure answer` IS ONE OF
    `no disclosure is required: the legal costs are not likely to exceed the disclosure threshold amount (s 307A)`
    `no disclosure is required: the client is a sophisticated client (s 311(1)(c)-(d))`
    `no disclosure is required: the client will not be required to pay the legal costs (s 311(1)(e))`
    `no disclosure is required, if the principal's decision that further disclosure is not warranted was made on reasonable grounds (s 311(1)(b))`
    `abbreviated disclosure under s 307B, or detailed disclosure under s 308; if there is no s 307B disclosure, s 308 applies`
    `detailed disclosure in writing under s 308`

DECLARE `Disclosure facts` HAS
    `the likely legal costs` IS A NUMBER
    `the client is a sophisticated client`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the client will not be required to pay` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a disclosure was received in the previous 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the client agreed in writing to waive disclosure`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a principal decided further disclosure is not warranted` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 307A "A law practice is not required to make a disclosure under this division for a matter if the total amount
-- of the legal costs in the matter, excluding disbursements and exclusive of GST, is not likely to exceed the
-- disclosure threshold amount."
-- s 307B(1) "A law practice may make a disclosure under this section for a matter if the total amount of the legal
-- costs ... is not likely to exceed the detailed disclosure threshold amount."
-- s 308(1) "This section applies ... if the total amount of the legal costs ... is likely to exceed the detailed
-- disclosure threshold amount." (2) "This section also applies ... if (a) the total amount ... is likely to exceed the
-- disclosure threshold amount; and (b) the law practice does not make a disclosure ... under section 307B."
-- s 311(1) "Disclosure under section 307B, 308 or 309(1) is not required to be made in any of the following
-- circumstances-- (b) if-- (i) the client has received 1 or more disclosures ... in the previous 12 months; and (ii) the
-- client has agreed in writing to waive the right to disclosure; and (iii) a principal of the law practice decides on
-- reasonable grounds that ... the further disclosure is not warranted; (c) if the client is-- [the listed kinds]; (d)
-- if the legal costs ... have ... been agreed as a result of a tender process; (e) if the client will not be required
-- to pay the legal costs or they will not otherwise be recovered by the law practice". (f), circumstances prescribed by
-- regulation, is not encoded (the regulation is not deposited).
-- "the legal costs" here are the likely total, excluding disbursements and GST, in dollars.
GIVEN `f` IS A `Disclosure facts`
GIVETH A `Disclosure answer`
`the disclosure answer (ss 307A-308, 311)` `f` MEANS
    IF `f`'s `the likely legal costs` AT MOST `the disclosure threshold amount (s 300)`
    THEN `no disclosure is required: the legal costs are not likely to exceed the disclosure threshold amount (s 307A)`
    ELSE IF `f`'s `the client is a sophisticated client`
         THEN `no disclosure is required: the client is a sophisticated client (s 311(1)(c)-(d))`
         ELSE IF `f`'s `the client will not be required to pay`
              THEN `no disclosure is required: the client will not be required to pay the legal costs (s 311(1)(e))`
              ELSE IF     `f`'s `a disclosure was received in the previous 12 months`
                      AND `f`'s `the client agreed in writing to waive disclosure`
                      AND `f`'s `a principal decided further disclosure is not warranted`
                   THEN `no disclosure is required, if the principal's decision that further disclosure is not warranted was made on reasonable grounds (s 311(1)(b))`
                   ELSE IF `f`'s `the likely legal costs` AT MOST `the detailed disclosure threshold amount (s 300)`
                        THEN `abbreviated disclosure under s 307B, or detailed disclosure under s 308; if there is no s 307B disclosure, s 308 applies`
                        ELSE `detailed disclosure in writing under s 308`

-- s 313(1) "If a costs agreement involves an uplift fee, the law practice must, before entering into the agreement,
-- disclose to the client in writing-- (a) the law practice's legal costs; and (b) the uplift fee, or the basis of
-- calculation of the uplift fee; and (c) the reasons why the uplift fee is warranted." (2) "A law practice is not
-- required to make a disclosure under subsection (1) to a sophisticated client."
-- An unmet "if" answers no (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)); s 313(2) is a flat negative.
GIVEN `the agreement involves an uplift fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sophisticated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the law practice must disclose the uplift fee in writing first (s 313)` `the agreement involves an uplift fee` `sophisticated` MEANS
    IF `the agreement involves an uplift fee` AND (NOT `sophisticated`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `Non-disclosure answer` IS ONE OF
    `s 316 does not hold back these costs: the law practice made every disclosure Division 3 required`
    `I need not pay these costs unless they have been assessed, and the law practice cannot sue me for them until then (s 316(1)-(2))`
    `the costs have been assessed, so s 316(1)-(2) no longer hold them back; the assessment may have reduced them for the failure (s 316(4))`
    `s 316(1)-(4) do not apply to the first law practice's own costs, to the extent its failure was caused by the retained law practice (s 316(5)(a))`

-- s 316(1) "If a law practice does not disclose to a client ... anything required by this division to be disclosed,
-- the client ... need not pay the legal costs unless they have been assessed under division 7." (2) "... may not
-- maintain proceedings against the client ... for the recovery of legal costs unless the costs have been assessed".
-- (4) "on an assessment ... the amount of the costs may be reduced by an amount considered by the costs assessor to be
-- proportionate to the seriousness of the failure to disclose." (5) "If a law practice retains another law practice
-- ... and the first law practice fails to disclose something to the client solely because the retained law practice
-- failed to disclose relevant information to the first law practice as required by section 309(2), then subsections
-- (1) to (4)-- (a) do not apply to the legal costs owing to the first law practice ... to the extent that the
-- non-disclosure ... was caused by the failure of the retained law practice ...; and (b) do apply to the legal costs
-- owing to the retained law practice."
GIVEN `the law practice failed to disclose something Division 3 required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure was solely because a law practice it retained did not tell it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs have been assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Non-disclosure answer`
`the s 316 answer` `the law practice failed to disclose something Division 3 required` `the failure was solely because a law practice it retained did not tell it` `the costs have been assessed` MEANS
    IF NOT `the law practice failed to disclose something Division 3 required`
    THEN `s 316 does not hold back these costs: the law practice made every disclosure Division 3 required`
    ELSE IF `the failure was solely because a law practice it retained did not tell it`
         THEN `s 316(1)-(4) do not apply to the first law practice's own costs, to the extent its failure was caused by the retained law practice (s 316(5)(a))`
         ELSE IF `the costs have been assessed`
              THEN `the costs have been assessed, so s 316(1)-(2) no longer hold them back; the assessment may have reduced them for the failure (s 316(4))`
              ELSE `I need not pay these costs unless they have been assessed, and the law practice cannot sue me for them until then (s 316(1)-(2))`

DECLARE `Report kind` IS ONE OF
    `a written report of the progress of the matter`
    `a written report of the legal costs incurred to date or since the last bill`

DECLARE `Report answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, on reasonable request; the law practice may charge a reasonable amount for it (s 317(1)(a), (2))`
    `yes, on reasonable request, and the law practice must not charge for it (s 317(1)(b), (2))`
    `no: a law practice need not give a report to a sophisticated client (s 317(5))`
    `not from this law practice: it was retained by my law practice, which must give me the report (s 317(3))`

-- s 317(1) "A law practice must give a client, on reasonable request-- (a) a written report of the progress of the
-- matter ...; and (b) a written report of the legal costs incurred by the client to date, or since the last bill".
-- (2) "A law practice may charge a client a reasonable amount for a report under subsection (1)(a) but must not
-- charge a client for a report under subsection (1)(b)." (3) "A law practice retained on behalf of a client by
-- another law practice is not required to give a report to the client ..." (4) "Subsection (3) does not apply if the
-- other law practice ceases to act for the client in the matter when the law practice is retained." (5) "A law
-- practice is not required to give a report under subsection (1) to a sophisticated client."
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Report kind`
      `sophisticated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `retained by my law practice, which still acts for me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Report answer`
`the s 317 answer` `the kind` `sophisticated` `retained by my law practice, which still acts for me` MEANS
    IF `sophisticated`
    THEN `no: a law practice need not give a report to a sophisticated client (s 317(5))`
    ELSE IF `retained by my law practice, which still acts for me`
         THEN `not from this law practice: it was retained by my law practice, which must give me the report (s 317(3))`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the kind`
              WHEN `a written report of the progress of the matter` THEN `yes, on reasonable request; the law practice may charge a reasonable amount for it (s 317(1)(a), (2))`
              WHEN `a written report of the legal costs incurred to date or since the last bill` THEN `yes, on reasonable request, and the law practice must not charge for it (s 317(1)(b), (2))`

§§ `Costs agreements (Division 5)`

-- s 300 "costs agreement means an agreement about the payment of legal costs." "conditional costs agreement means a
-- costs agreement that provides that the payment of some or all of the legal costs is conditional on the successful
-- outcome of the matter ...". "uplift fee means additional legal costs, excluding disbursements, payable under a costs
-- agreement on the successful outcome of the matter". An agreement with an uplift fee is therefore one whose payment
-- of some legal costs is conditional on success, and so a conditional costs agreement.
DECLARE `Costs agreement facts` HAS
    `written or evidenced in writing`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `made by accepting a written offer`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offer states what s 322(4) requires`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `says the costs are not subject to costs assessment`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment depends on a successful outcome`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the matter involves criminal or Family Law Act proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sets out what counts as a successful outcome`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `in writing`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `in clear plain language`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed by the client`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the client was told of the right to independent legal advice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `cooling-off clear business days`                         IS A NUMBER
    `provides for an uplift fee`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains an estimate or range of the uplift fee`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the matter is litigious`                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the uplift fee amount`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `the undiscounted legal costs otherwise payable`          IS A NUMBER
    `the amount is calculated by reference to the award, settlement or property recovered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreement adopts an applicable scale of costs`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the client's interest in the proceedings passes to the law practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the client is sophisticated`                             IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Contravention` IS ONE OF
    `not written or evidenced in writing (s 322(2))`
    `the offer does not clearly state what s 322(4) requires`
    `it says the costs are not subject to costs assessment (s 322(5))`
    `a conditional costs agreement in a matter involving criminal or Family Law Act proceedings (s 323(2))`
    `it does not set out what counts as a successful outcome (s 323(3)(a))`
    `a conditional costs agreement not in writing (s 323(3)(c)(i))`
    `a conditional costs agreement not in clear plain language (s 323(3)(c)(ii))`
    `a conditional costs agreement not signed by the client (s 323(3)(c)(iii))`
    `no statement that the client was told of the right to independent legal advice (s 323(3)(d))`
    `a cooling-off period of less than 5 clear business days (s 323(3)(e))`
    `the basis of the uplift fee is not separately identified (s 324(2))`
    `no estimate, or range of estimates, of the uplift fee (s 324(3))`
    `the uplift fee is more than 25% of the legal costs otherwise payable (s 324(4))`
    `a contingency fee: the amount is calculated by reference to the award, settlement or property recovered (s 325(1))`
    `the client's interest in the proceedings is transferred to the law practice (s 325(3))`

GIVEN `f` IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a conditional costs agreement (s 300)` `f` IF
    `f`'s `payment depends on a successful outcome` OR `f`'s `provides for an uplift fee`

GIVEN `it is so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the item` IS A `Contravention`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Contravention`
`listed if` `it is so` `the item` MEANS
    IF `it is so` THEN LIST `the item` ELSE EMPTY

-- s 324(4) "If a conditional costs agreement relates to a litigious matter, the uplift fee must not exceed 25% of the
-- legal costs, excluding disbursements, otherwise payable." (5) "... if a law practice does discount its fees, the
-- reference in subsection (4) to legal costs is the fees the law practice would have charged if the law practice's
-- fees had not been discounted." Not litigious: s 324(4) sets no cap (an unmet "if"), answered NOTHING.
GIVEN `f` IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the most uplift fee allowed (s 324(4)-(5))` `f` MEANS
    IF `f`'s `the matter is litigious`
    THEN JUST (`f`'s `the undiscounted legal costs otherwise payable` TIMES `the uplift cap (s 324(4))`)
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `f` IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the uplift fee is over the cap (s 324(4))` `f` IF
    CONSIDER `the most uplift fee allowed (s 324(4)-(5))` `f`
    WHEN JUST `the cap` THEN `f`'s `the uplift fee amount` GREATER THAN `the cap`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- s 322(2) "The costs agreement must be written or evidenced in writing." (3)-(4) an agreement may consist of a written
-- offer that "must clearly state-- (a) that it is an offer to enter into a costs agreement; and (b) that the offer can
-- be accepted in writing or by other conduct; and (c) the type of conduct that will constitute acceptance." (5)
-- "Except as provided by section 344, a costs agreement can not provide that the legal costs ... are not subject to
-- costs assessment" (s 344: a sophisticated client may contract out of division 7).
-- s 323(2) "A conditional costs agreement may relate to any matter, except a matter that involves criminal proceedings
-- or proceedings under the Family Law Act 1975 (Cwlth)." (3) "A conditional costs agreement-- (a) must set out the
-- circumstances that constitute the successful outcome ...; (c) must be-- (i) in writing; and (ii) in clear plain
-- language; and (iii) signed by the client; and (d) must contain a statement that the client has been informed of the
-- client's right to seek independent legal advice ...; and (e) must contain a cooling-off period of not less than 5
-- clear business days ..." (4) "Subsection (3)(c)(iii), (d) and (e) do not apply to ... (b) a conditional costs
-- agreement made with a sophisticated client." ((4)(a), agreements between law practices, is not the client's case.)
-- s 324(2) "The basis of calculation of the uplift fee must be separately identified in the agreement." (3) "The
-- agreement must contain an estimate of the uplift fee or, if that is not reasonably practicable, both of the
-- following-- (a) a range of estimates of the uplift fee; (b) an explanation of the major variables ...". (4) the cap.
-- s 325(1) "A law practice must not enter into a costs agreement under which the amount payable to the law practice,
-- or any part of that amount, is calculated by reference to the amount of any award or settlement or the value of any
-- property that may be recovered in any proceedings to which the agreement relates." (2) "Subsection (1) does not
-- apply to the extent that the costs agreement adopts an applicable scale of costs." (3) "A law practice must not enter
-- into a costs agreement under which all or part of the client's interest in any proceedings ... is transferred to the
-- law practice instead of the client being required to pay an amount payable to the law practice."
GIVEN `f` IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Contravention`
`the Division 5 contraventions` `f` MEANS
    concat (LIST
        `listed if` (NOT (`f`'s `written or evidenced in writing`)) `not written or evidenced in writing (s 322(2))`,
        `listed if` (`f`'s `made by accepting a written offer` AND (NOT (`f`'s `the offer states what s 322(4) requires`))) `the offer does not clearly state what s 322(4) requires`,
        `listed if` (`f`'s `says the costs are not subject to costs assessment` AND (NOT (`f`'s `the client is sophisticated`))) `it says the costs are not subject to costs assessment (s 322(5))`,
        `listed if` (`conditional` AND `f`'s `the matter involves criminal or Family Law Act proceedings`) `a conditional costs agreement in a matter involving criminal or Family Law Act proceedings (s 323(2))`,
        `listed if` (`conditional` AND (NOT (`f`'s `sets out what counts as a successful outcome`))) `it does not set out what counts as a successful outcome (s 323(3)(a))`,
        `listed if` (`conditional` AND (NOT (`f`'s `in writing`))) `a conditional costs agreement not in writing (s 323(3)(c)(i))`,
        `listed if` (`conditional` AND (NOT (`f`'s `in clear plain language`))) `a conditional costs agreement not in clear plain language (s 323(3)(c)(ii))`,
        `listed if` (`conditional with a client who is not sophisticated` AND (NOT (`f`'s `signed by the client`))) `a conditional costs agreement not signed by the client (s 323(3)(c)(iii))`,
        `listed if` (`conditional with a client who is not sophisticated` AND (NOT (`f`'s `states the client was told of the right to independent legal advice`))) `no statement that the client was told of the right to independent legal advice (s 323(3)(d))`,
        `listed if` (`conditional with a client who is not sophisticated` AND `f`'s `cooling-off clear business days` LESS THAN 5) `a cooling-off period of less than 5 clear business days (s 323(3)(e))`,
        `listed if` (`f`'s `provides for an uplift fee` AND (NOT (`f`'s `the basis of the uplift fee is separately identified`))) `the basis of the uplift fee is not separately identified (s 324(2))`,
        `listed if` (`f`'s `provides for an uplift fee` AND (NOT (`f`'s `contains an estimate or range of the uplift fee`))) `no estimate, or range of estimates, of the uplift fee (s 324(3))`,
        `listed if` (`f`'s `provides for an uplift fee` AND `the uplift fee is over the cap (s 324(4))` `f`) `the uplift fee is more than 25% of the legal costs otherwise payable (s 324(4))`,
        `listed if` (`f`'s `the amount is calculated by reference to the award, settlement or property recovered` AND (NOT (`f`'s `the agreement adopts an applicable scale of costs`))) `a contingency fee: the amount is calculated by reference to the award, settlement or property recovered (s 325(1))`,
        `listed if` (`f`'s `the client's interest in the proceedings passes to the law practice`) `the client's interest in the proceedings is transferred to the law practice (s 325(3))`)
    WHERE
        `conditional` MEANS `is a conditional costs agreement (s 300)` `f`
        `conditional with a client who is not sophisticated` MEANS `conditional` AND (NOT (`f`'s `the client is sophisticated`))

GIVEN `c` IS A `Contravention`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a contravention of s 324` `c` IF
        `c` EQUALS `the basis of the uplift fee is not separately identified (s 324(2))`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `no estimate, or range of estimates, of the uplift fee (s 324(3))`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `the uplift fee is more than 25% of the legal costs otherwise payable (s 324(4))`

GIVEN `c` IS A `Contravention`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a contravention of s 325` `c` IF
        `c` EQUALS `a contingency fee: the amount is calculated by reference to the award, settlement or property recovered (s 325(1))`
    OR  `c` EQUALS `the client's interest in the proceedings is transferred to the law practice (s 325(3))`

DECLARE `Void answer` IS ONE OF
    `not void under s 327(1) on these facts: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Divisions 5 and 7 (s 326)`
    `void (s 327(1)): the law practice may recover costs only under the applicable scale or at fair and reasonable value, and never more than the agreement would have given it; any excess must be repaid (s 327(2)-(3))`
    `void (s 327(1)), and the law practice may not recover any of the uplift fee and must repay any uplift fee received; other costs only under the scale or at fair and reasonable value, capped at the agreement (s 327(2)-(4))`
    `void (s 327(1)), and the law practice may recover nothing for its legal services in the matter and must repay everything received for them (s 327(5))`

-- s 326 "Subject to this division and division 7, a costs agreement may be enforced in the same way as any other
-- contract." s 327(1) "A costs agreement that contravenes, or is entered into in contravention of, any provision of
-- this division is void." (2) "... legal costs under a void costs agreement are recoverable as set out in section
-- 319(1)(b) or (c)" [the applicable scale of costs, or else the fair and reasonable value]. (3) "However, a law
-- practice is not entitled to recover ... any amount in excess of the amount the law practice would have been entitled
-- to recover if the costs agreement had not been void and must repay any excess amount received." (4) "A law practice
-- that has entered into a costs agreement in contravention of section 324 is not entitled to recover the whole or any
-- part of the uplift fee and must repay the amount received ..." (5) "A law practice that has entered into a costs
-- agreement in contravention of section 325 is not entitled to recover any amount relating to the provision of legal
-- services in the matter ... and must repay any amount received ..." (6) the person may recover the repayment "as a
-- debt in a court of competent jurisdiction".
GIVEN `f` IS A `Costs agreement facts`
GIVETH A `Void answer`
`the s 327 answer` `f` MEANS
    IF null `the contraventions`
    THEN `not void under s 327(1) on these facts: it may be enforced like any other contract, subject to Divisions 5 and 7 (s 326)`
    ELSE IF any `is a contravention of s 325` `the contraventions`
         THEN `void (s 327(1)), and the law practice may recover nothing for its legal services in the matter and must repay everything received for them (s 327(5))`
         ELSE IF any `is a contravention of s 324` `the contraventions`
              THEN `void (s 327(1)), and the law practice may not recover any of the uplift fee and must repay any uplift fee received; other costs only under the scale or at fair and reasonable value, capped at the agreement (s 327(2)-(4))`
              ELSE `void (s 327(1)): the law practice may recover costs only under the applicable scale or at fair and reasonable value, and never more than the agreement would have given it; any excess must be repaid (s 327(2)-(3))`
    WHERE
        `the contraventions` MEANS `the Division 5 contraventions` `f`

DECLARE `Cooling-off answer` IS ONE OF
    `s 323 gives no cooling-off: this is not a conditional costs agreement`
    `s 323(3)(e) does not apply to a sophisticated client (s 323(4)(b)); any cooling-off is only what the agreement says`
    `the agreement is void: its cooling-off period is shorter than 5 clear business days (ss 323(3)(e), 327(1))`
    `yes: I may terminate by written notice; the law practice may then recover only the costs of work done before termination on my instructions and with my knowledge that it would be done in the period, and no uplift fee (s 323(5))`
    `no: the cooling-off period in the agreement has ended`

-- s 323(3)(e) "must contain a cooling-off period of not less than 5 clear business days during which the client, by
-- written notice, may terminate the agreement." (5) "If a client terminates an agreement within the period ..., the law
-- practice-- (a) may recover only those legal costs for legal services performed for the client before that
-- termination that were performed on the instructions of the client and with the client's knowledge that the legal
-- services would be performed during that period; and (b) ... may not recover the uplift fee (if any)."
-- Reading: the period runs from the day after the agreement is made; a notice is within it if fewer than the period's
-- business days have ended before the day the notice is given.
GIVEN `conditional` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sophisticated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `cooling-off days in the agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `business days ended before the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Cooling-off answer`
`the s 323 cooling-off answer` `conditional` `sophisticated` `cooling-off days in the agreement` `business days ended before the notice` MEANS
    IF NOT `conditional`
    THEN `s 323 gives no cooling-off: this is not a conditional costs agreement`
    ELSE IF `sophisticated`
         THEN `s 323(3)(e) does not apply to a sophisticated client (s 323(4)(b)); any cooling-off is only what the agreement says`
         ELSE IF `cooling-off days in the agreement` LESS THAN 5
              THEN `the agreement is void: its cooling-off period is shorter than 5 clear business days (ss 323(3)(e), 327(1))`
              ELSE IF `business days ended before the notice` LESS THAN `cooling-off days in the agreement`
                   THEN `yes: I may terminate by written notice; the law practice may then recover only the costs of work done before termination on my instructions and with my knowledge that it would be done in the period, and no uplift fee (s 323(5))`
                   ELSE `no: the cooling-off period in the agreement has ended`

DECLARE `Set aside answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I may apply to the Supreme Court or QCAT, which may set the agreement aside if satisfied it is not fair or reasonable; it may then order what I pay, but not more than the agreement would have allowed (s 328(1), (4)-(6))`
    `no: only a client (a person to whom or for whom the legal services are or were provided), or an associated third party payer that is a party to the agreement, may apply (ss 322(6), 328(1), (10))`

-- s 328(1) "On application by a client, the Supreme Court or the tribunal may order that a costs agreement be set aside
-- if satisfied the agreement is not fair or reasonable." (6) "... may not order the payment of an amount in excess of
-- the amount the law practice would have been entitled to recover if the costs agreement had not been set aside."
-- (10) "client means a person to whom or for whom legal services are or have been provided." s 322(6) extends s 328 to
-- an associated third party payer that is party to the agreement. A failure to disclose is one matter the court may
-- weigh (s 328(2)(c)); s 316(3) says the client "may also apply". Whether it is "not fair or reasonable" is the court's
-- or tribunal's judgment, so the answer is conditional.
GIVEN `a person entitled to apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Set aside answer`
`the s 328 answer` `a person entitled to apply` MEANS
    IF `a person entitled to apply`
    THEN `yes: I may apply to the Supreme Court or QCAT, which may set the agreement aside if satisfied it is not fair or reasonable; it may then order what I pay, but not more than the agreement would have allowed (s 328(1), (4)-(6))`
    ELSE `no: only a client (a person to whom or for whom the legal services are or were provided), or an associated third party payer that is a party to the agreement, may apply (ss 322(6), 328(1), (10))`

§§ `Interest (s 321)`

DECLARE `Interest answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: the bill does not state that interest is payable and the rate (s 321(2))`
    `no: the rate is more than the rate prescribed by regulation (s 321(3))`
    `yes, under the costs agreement (s 321(1)(a))`
    `yes: the costs have been unpaid 30 days or more after the bill (s 321(1)(b))`
    `not yet: interest can run only once the costs are unpaid 30 days after the bill, from` HAS `the first day` IS A DATE

-- s 321(1) "A law practice may charge interest on unpaid legal costs-- (a) if a costs agreement provides for charging
-- interest on unpaid legal costs--under the costs agreement; or (b) otherwise--if the costs are unpaid 30 days or more
-- after the law practice has given a bill for the costs under this part." (2) "However, a law practice must not charge
-- interest under subsection (1) on unpaid legal costs unless the bill for the costs contains a statement that interest
-- is payable and of the rate of interest." (3) "A law practice may not charge interest under this section, including
-- under a costs agreement, at a rate that is more than the rate prescribed under a regulation."
-- The prescribed maximum rate is an input: the regulation is not deposited.
GIVEN `the costs agreement provides for interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the bill was given` IS A DATE
      `the bill states interest is payable and the rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate charged` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed maximum rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Interest answer`
`the s 321 answer` `the costs agreement provides for interest` `the day the bill was given` `the bill states interest is payable and the rate` `the rate charged` `the prescribed maximum rate` `the day asked about` MEANS
    IF NOT `the bill states interest is payable and the rate`
    THEN `no: the bill does not state that interest is payable and the rate (s 321(2))`
    ELSE IF `the rate charged` GREATER THAN `the prescribed maximum rate`
         THEN `no: the rate is more than the rate prescribed by regulation (s 321(3))`
         ELSE IF `the costs agreement provides for interest`
              THEN `yes, under the costs agreement (s 321(1)(a))`
              ELSE IF `the 30th day` `is no later than` `the day asked about`
                   THEN `yes: the costs have been unpaid 30 days or more after the bill (s 321(1)(b))`
                   ELSE `not yet: interest can run only once the costs are unpaid 30 days after the bill, from` `the 30th day`
    WHERE
        `the 30th day` MEANS `the day` 30 `days after` `the day the bill was given`

§§ `Billing (Division 6)`

DECLARE `Costs party` IS ONE OF `the law practice`, `the client`
DECLARE `Costs act` IS ONE OF
    `give the itemised bill`
    `start proceedings to recover the legal costs`

-- s 332(2) "The law practice must comply with the request within 28 days after the date on which the request is made."
-- Day 0: the day of the request. (6) "A law practice is not entitled to charge a person for the preparation of an
-- itemised bill requested under this section."
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Costs party` `Costs act`
`s 332(2) -- the law practice must give the itemised bill within 28 days after the request` MEANS
    PARTY `the law practice`
    MUST  `give the itemised bill`
    WITHIN 28
    LEST  BREACH BY `the law practice` BECAUSE "s 332(2): the itemised bill was not given within 28 days after the request"

-- s 329(1) "A law practice must not start legal proceedings to recover legal costs from a person until at least 30
-- days after the law practice has given a bill to the person under sections 330 and 331". s 332(4) the same for a lump
-- sum bill. Day 0: the day the bill was given; day 30 is the first day proceedings may start, so the prohibition runs
-- through day 29. (3) "A court ... before which any proceedings are brought in contravention of subsection (1) must stay
-- those proceedings".
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Costs party` `Costs act`
`s 329(1) -- the law practice must not start recovery proceedings until 30 days after the bill` MEANS
    PARTY `the law practice`
    SHANT `start proceedings to recover the legal costs`
    WITHIN 29
    LEST  BREACH BY `the law practice` BECAUSE "s 329(1): proceedings to recover legal costs were started less than 30 days after the bill was given; the court must stay them (s 329(3))"

DECLARE `Itemised bill answer` IS ONE OF
    `s 332 gives no right to an itemised bill: the bill I was given is already itemised`
    `the law practice must give it to me free of charge by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `it was given in time (s 332(2))`
    `the law practice is late: it had to give it to me by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

-- s 332(1) "If a bill is given by a law practice in the form of a lump sum bill, any person who is entitled to apply
-- for an assessment of the legal costs to which the bill relates may request the law practice to give the person an
-- itemised bill." (2) within 28 days after the request. The client may always apply for an assessment (s 335(1)); the
-- 12-month limit of s 335(5) is not read into s 332(1) (NOTES.md, fork line 3).
GIVEN `the bill was a lump sum bill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I asked for the itemised bill` IS A DATE
      `the itemised bill has been given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the itemised bill was given` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Itemised bill answer`
`the s 332 answer` `the bill was a lump sum bill` `the day I asked for the itemised bill` `the itemised bill has been given` `the day the itemised bill was given` `the day asked about` MEANS
    IF NOT `the bill was a lump sum bill`
    THEN `s 332 gives no right to an itemised bill: the bill I was given is already itemised`
    ELSE IF `the itemised bill has been given`
         THEN IF `the day the itemised bill was given` `is no later than` `the 28th day`
              THEN `it was given in time (s 332(2))`
              ELSE `the law practice is late: it had to give it to me by` `the 28th day`
         ELSE IF `the day asked about` `is no later than` `the 28th day`
              THEN `the law practice must give it to me free of charge by` `the 28th day`
              ELSE `the law practice is late: it had to give it to me by` `the 28th day`
    WHERE
        `the 28th day` MEANS `the day` 28 `days after` `the day I asked for the itemised bill`

DECLARE `Recovery answer` IS ONE OF
    `not yet: the law practice must first give me a bill (s 329(1))`
    `not until the costs have been assessed: the law practice did not make the disclosures Division 3 required (s 316(2))`
    `not until the costs assessment is completed, unless the court gives leave (s 338(b))`
    `not until 30 days after it gives me the itemised bill I asked for (s 332(5))`
    `not before` HAS `the first day` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Recovery facts` HAS
    `bill given`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `bill day`            IS A DATE
    `lump sum bill`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `itemised bill asked for`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `itemised bill request day` IS A DATE
    `itemised bill given`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `itemised bill day`   IS A DATE
    `disclosure failure not yet assessed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `costs application pending`        IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 329(1) [above]; s 332(4) "Subject to subsection (5), a law practice must not commence legal proceedings to
-- recover legal costs from a person who has been given a lump sum bill until at least 30 days after the date on which
-- the person is given the bill." (5) "If the person makes a request for an itemised bill within 30 days after receiving
-- the lump sum bill, the law practice must not commence proceedings ... until 30 days after complying with the
-- request." s 338 "If a costs application is made-- (a) a person liable for the legal costs ... can not be required to
-- pay money into court on account of the legal costs; and (b) subject to the leave of the court, the law practice must
-- not start any proceedings to recover the legal costs until the costs assessment has been completed." s 316(2) [above].
-- s 329(2) (a court may authorise proceedings sooner if the person is about to leave the jurisdiction) is a court's
-- order, not encoded.
GIVEN `f` IS A `Recovery facts`
GIVETH A `Recovery answer`
`the earliest recovery proceedings answer (ss 316(2), 329, 332, 338)` `f` MEANS
    IF NOT (`f`'s `bill given`)
    THEN `not yet: the law practice must first give me a bill (s 329(1))`
    ELSE IF `f`'s `disclosure failure not yet assessed`
         THEN `not until the costs have been assessed: the law practice did not make the disclosures Division 3 required (s 316(2))`
         ELSE IF `f`'s `costs application pending`
              THEN `not until the costs assessment is completed, unless the court gives leave (s 338(b))`
              ELSE IF `the s 332(5) wait applies`
                   THEN IF `f`'s `itemised bill given`
                        THEN `not before` (`the day` 30 `days after` (`f`'s `itemised bill day`))
                        ELSE `not until 30 days after it gives me the itemised bill I asked for (s 332(5))`
                   ELSE `not before` (`the day` 30 `days after` (`f`'s `bill day`))
    WHERE
        `the s 332(5) wait applies` MEANS
                `f`'s `lump sum bill`
            AND `f`'s `itemised bill asked for`
            AND (`f`'s `itemised bill request day` `is no later than` (`the day` 30 `days after` (`f`'s `bill day`)))

§§ `Costs assessment (Division 7)`

DECLARE `Assessment time answer` IS ONE OF
    `no time limit has started: there has been no bill, request for payment or payment`
    `in time: I may apply up to and including` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `out of time, but a costs assessor or the court may still deal with it after considering my reasons for the delay (s 335(6)); the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `out of time, and as a sophisticated client a late application cannot be dealt with under s 335(6); the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE

-- s 335(1) "A client may apply for an assessment of the whole or any part of legal costs." (3) "... even if the legal
-- costs have been wholly or partly paid." (5) "A costs application by a client or a third party payer must be made
-- within 12 months after-- (a) the bill was given, or the request for payment was made, to the client or third party
-- payer; or (b) the costs were paid if neither a bill was given nor a request was made." (6) "However, a costs
-- application made out of time, otherwise than by any of the following, may be dealt with by a costs assessor or a
-- court if, under the Uniform Civil Procedure Rules, the assessor or the court decides to deal with it after
-- considering the reasons for delay-- (a) a sophisticated client; (b) [a sophisticated third party payer]."
GIVEN `a bill was given or payment was requested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the bill or request` IS A DATE
      `the costs have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the costs were paid` IS A DATE
      `sophisticated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Assessment time answer`
`the s 335 answer` `a bill was given or payment was requested` `the day of the bill or request` `the costs have been paid` `the day the costs were paid` `sophisticated` `the day of the application` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a bill was given or payment was requested`) AND (NOT `the costs have been paid`)
    THEN `no time limit has started: there has been no bill, request for payment or payment`
    ELSE IF `the day of the application` `is no later than` `the last day`
         THEN `in time: I may apply up to and including` `the last day`
         ELSE IF `sophisticated`
              THEN `out of time, and as a sophisticated client a late application cannot be dealt with under s 335(6); the last day was` `the last day`
              ELSE `out of time, but a costs assessor or the court may still deal with it after considering my reasons for the delay (s 335(6)); the last day was` `the last day`
    WHERE
        `the start` MEANS
            IF `a bill was given or payment was requested`
            THEN `the day of the bill or request`
            ELSE `the day the costs were paid`
        `the last day` MEANS `the day` 12 `months after` `the start`

DECLARE `Agreement assessment answer` IS ONE OF
    `the costs assessor must assess the disputed costs by the costs agreement (s 340(1))`
    `s 340 does not tie the assessment to the agreement: no provision of it fixes the amount, or a rate or other means of calculating it (s 340(1)(a))`
    `s 340 does not tie the assessment to the agreement: it has been set aside under s 328 (s 340(1)(b))`
    `not by the agreement: the assessor is satisfied of a material disclosure failure, that Division 5 precludes recovery, or the parties agree otherwise (s 340(1)(c)-(e)); the costs are assessed as fair and reasonable (s 341)`

-- s 340(1) "A costs assessor ... must assess any disputed costs that are subject to a costs agreement by reference to
-- the provisions of the costs agreement if-- (a) a relevant provision of the costs agreement specifies the amount, or a
-- rate or other means for calculating the amount, of the costs; and (b) the agreement has not been set aside under
-- section 328; unless the costs assessor is satisfied that-- (c) the costs agreement does not comply in a material
-- respect with any disclosure requirements of division 3; or (d) division 5 precludes the law practice concerned from
-- recovering the amount of the costs; or (e) the parties otherwise agree." (2) "The costs assessor is not required to
-- initiate an examination of the matters mentioned in subsection (1)(c) and (d)." The assessor's being satisfied is an
-- input.
GIVEN `the agreement fixes the amount or a rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement has been set aside` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessor is satisfied an exception in s 340(1)(c)-(e) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Agreement assessment answer`
`the s 340 answer` `the agreement fixes the amount or a rate` `the agreement has been set aside` `the assessor is satisfied an exception in s 340(1)(c)-(e) applies` MEANS
    IF NOT `the agreement fixes the amount or a rate`
    THEN `s 340 does not tie the assessment to the agreement: no provision of it fixes the amount, or a rate or other means of calculating it (s 340(1)(a))`
    ELSE IF `the agreement has been set aside`
         THEN `s 340 does not tie the assessment to the agreement: it has been set aside under s 328 (s 340(1)(b))`
         ELSE IF `the assessor is satisfied an exception in s 340(1)(c)-(e) applies`
              THEN `not by the agreement: the assessor is satisfied of a material disclosure failure, that Division 5 precludes recovery, or the parties agree otherwise (s 340(1)(c)-(e)); the costs are assessed as fair and reasonable (s 341)`
              ELSE `the costs assessor must assess the disputed costs by the costs agreement (s 340(1))`

DECLARE `Assessment costs answer` IS ONE OF
    `the law practice pays the costs of the assessment, unless the costs assessor orders otherwise (s 342(2))`
    `whoever the costs assessor orders pays the costs of the assessment (s 342(3))`

-- s 342(2) "Unless the costs assessor otherwise orders, the law practice to which the legal costs are payable or were
-- paid must pay the costs of the costs assessment if-- (a) on the assessment, the legal costs are reduced by 15% or
-- more; or (b) the costs assessor is satisfied the law practice failed to comply with division 3." (3) "... if, under
-- subsection (2), the law practice is not liable to pay the costs of the costs assessment, the costs of the assessment
-- must be paid by the party ordered by the costs assessor to pay those costs."
-- The reduction is measured against the legal costs as billed (the amount assessed), in dollars.
GIVEN `the legal costs claimed` IS A NUMBER
      `the legal costs as assessed` IS A NUMBER
      `the assessor is satisfied the law practice failed to comply with Division 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Assessment costs answer`
`the s 342 answer` `the legal costs claimed` `the legal costs as assessed` `the assessor is satisfied the law practice failed to comply with Division 3` MEANS
    IF     (`the legal costs claimed` MINUS `the legal costs as assessed`) AT LEAST (`the legal costs claimed` TIMES `the assessment reduction mark (s 342(2)(a))`)
        OR `the assessor is satisfied the law practice failed to comply with Division 3`
    THEN `the law practice pays the costs of the assessment, unless the costs assessor orders otherwise (s 342(2))`
    ELSE `whoever the costs assessor orders pays the costs of the assessment (s 342(3))`
